    "description": "make train's book texts, pinned (picovox_train/books.py): each Project Gutenberg text the recipe reads - the heteronym labels' books (data/nn/train.json context.labels texts) and the distillation's (distill.targets texts) - by its name in the books directory (<name>.txt): its Gutenberg id, its source URL, the SHA-256 and size of its bytes as fetched (what the pipeline reads), the date it was pinned (fetched), its Gutenberg revision (the header's 'Most recently updated' date), and a Wayback Machine capture of the source URL with the same bytes (null if none is known) - the fetch's fallback when Gutenberg has revised the book. The pins are the texts the shipped models were trained on: lib/models/g2pModel.js's context labels (fetched 2026-10-15) and the first full make train's distillation (lib/models/voiceModel.js - fetched 2026-10-16, after Gutenberg revised pg2554, so its pg2554 is pg2554-2026-10-16). A text whose hash doesn't match is never used: the fetch fails with how to restore it or re-pin it (python -m picovox_train.books pin NAME, then retrain).",
